{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevKKxL17jiXmUP7XJAw9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All existing tests pass. Now I have enough information to proceed with design.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and include a `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field in the Order data class.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt**: No changes needed - the existing save/findById/existsById methods support the cancel operation.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: In the create method, before saving the shipment, check if the order is CANCELLED. If so, throw `ConflictException` with a new error code `ORDER_CANCELLED`.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum.\n\n6. **OrderController.kt**: Add a new endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` that:\n   - Finds the order by ID (throw 404 if not found)\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, return it successfully (idempotent)\n   - Check all shipments for this order; if any is CONFIRMED, throw 409 and change nothing\n   - Otherwise, set order status to CANCELLED, save it, and cancel all CREATED shipments\n   - Return the cancelled order\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order successfully\n   - Cancelling an already CANCELLED order (idempotent success)\n   - Rejecting cancel when a CONFIRMED shipment exists (409, nothing changes)\n   - Rejecting cancel for non-existent order (404)\n\n**Alternative rejected and why:**\n- **Alternative 1**: Instead of adding a method to find shipments by orderId in ShipmentRepository, could pass ShipmentRepository to OrderController and inject it. This adds complexity since OrderController would need both repositories. The cleaner approach is to have ShipmentRepository provide a findByOrderId method, which is a natural extension of the repository pattern.\n- **Alternative 2**: Could handle the order status directly in the controller, but this violates separation of concerns. The status should be part of the entity and repository layer.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Happy path - cancel ACTIVE order**:\n   - Read: OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → Order(status=ACTIVE)\n   - Read: ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(orderId) → [Shipment(status=CREATED)]\n   - Write: Set Order.status = CANCELLED\n   - Write: OrderRepository.save(order) \n   - Write: Set Shipment.status = CANCELLED for each CREATED shipment\n   - Write: ShipmentRepository.save(shipment) for each\n   - Return: ResponseEntity with cancelled Order\n\n2. **Idempotent case - cancel already CANCELLED order**:\n   - Read: OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → Order(status=CANCELLED)\n   - Return: ResponseEntity with Order (success, unchanged)\n\n3. **Blocked case - CONFIRMED shipment exists**:\n   - Read: OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → Order(status=ACTIVE)\n   - Read: ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(orderId) → [Shipment(status=CONFIRMED)]\n   - Throw: ConflictException (409, ORDER_ALREADY_CONFIRMED or similar)\n   - Result: Nothing is written, Order and Shipments unchanged\n\n4. **Not found case**:\n   - Read: OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → null\n   - Throw: ResourceNotFoundException (404, ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n\n5. **Create shipment for CANCELLED order**:\n   - Read: OrderRepository.findById(request.orderId) → Order(status=CANCELLED)\n   - Throw: ConflictException (409, ORDER_CANCELLED)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: Cancel an ACTIVE order → returns 200, order status is CANCELLED, CREATED shipments are CANCELLED\n- Test 2: Cancel an already CANCELLED order → returns 200, order unchanged\n- Test 3: Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment → returns 409, order status remains ACTIVE, all shipments unchanged\n- Test 4: Cancel non-existent order → returns 404\n- Test 5: Create shipment for CANCELLED order → returns 409\n- Test 6: Create shipment for non-existent order → returns current behavior (allowed for now, per spec)\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2238,"cache_read_input_tokens":24575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2238},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"930e99ff-80c9-4730-ad69-da61901906c4","uuid":"4350ceb7-4ffd-4d6c-b1ec-784e6031d466","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:33:03.952Z","request_id":"req_011CevKKwar6hDQ5PiYgTCsV"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevKKxL17jiXmUP7XJAw9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ViX5QiSPNdau689bfiG7nN","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/var/folders/jr/lwzz65cx5pndqqdgzhnym1pc0000gn/T/observatory-run-c0589938-4a31-43f0-8a99-d250e6697019/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt","old_string":"import java.math.BigDecimal\n\n/**\n * An order placed by a customer.\n *\n * This is the baseline (pre-benchmark) shape. BE-002 asks an agent to reject orders\n * whose amount is not positive; the baseline deliberately accepts any amount.\n */\ndata class Order(\n    val orderId: String,\n    val customerId: String,\n    val amount: BigDecimal,\n    val currency: String,\n)","new_string":"import java.math.BigDecimal\n\n/**\n * The lifecycle of an order.\n *\n * [CANCELLED] is terminal. A cancelled order cannot have new shipments created.\n */\nenum class OrderStatus {\n    ACTIVE,\n    CANCELLED,\n}\n\n/**\n * An order placed by a customer.\n *\n * This is the baseline (pre-benchmark) shape. BE-002 asks an agent to reject orders\n * whose amount is not positive; the baseline deliberately accepts any amount.\n */\ndata class Order(\n    val orderId: String,\n    val customerId: String,\n    val amount: BigDecimal,\n    val currency: String,\n    val status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE,\n)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2238,"cache_read_input_tokens":24575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2238},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"930e99ff-80c9-4730-ad69-da61901906c4","uuid":"f252e255-ea90-48ef-b6fa-4ed863e992c3","tim